# Multi-stage AI content pipeline: Image vs Video prompts

## QUALITY LOCK (always enforce)

All image and video prompts MUST respect:

- **Character consistency** — same face, same body proportions, same outfit across frame and sequence.
- **Realistic physics** — cloth, motion, impact behave believably.
- **Cinematic motion** — professional film quality, no distortion, no cartoon.
- **High realism** — photorealistic, professional film quality.

Apply regardless of purpose type. No exceptions unless the user explicitly asks for stylized/cartoon.

---

## PURPOSE TYPES (classify and optimize per intent)

Use to route and tailor prompts. One primary type per request:

| Type | Use when |
|------|----------|
| **FIGHT / WAR / ACTION** | Combat, brawl, battle, stunt, violence, weapons. |
| **ADVERTISEMENT / PROMOTION** | Product, brand, commercial, promo clip. |
| **TALKING / CHAT / PODCAST** | Dialogue, interview, vlog, speaking to camera. |
| **STORY / CINEMATIC SCENE** | Narrative moment, film scene, dramatic beat. |
| **SOCIAL MEDIA PORTRAIT** | Profile shot, portrait, selfie-style, presence. |
| **THREAT / INTIMIDATION** | Menacing, warning, standoff, tension. |
| **HERO SHOT / ICONIC POSE** | Power pose, reveal, poster moment, iconic frame. |

Optimize image and video prompts for the detected purpose (e.g. FIGHT → wide shot, impact, enemy reaction; HERO SHOT → iconic pose, dramatic lighting; TALKING → stable frame, face focus).

